<title>SPAIN: Andalucia parliament bans MPs' mobile telephones.</title>
<headline>Andalucia parliament bans MPs' mobile telephones.</headline>
<dateline>SEVILLE, Spain 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The regional parliament of Andalucia in southern Spain on Wednesday banned members from using mobile telephones during meetings because it was fed up with the incessant ringing.</p>
<p>The ban applied to all meetings -- committees and plenary sessions -- and to officials, deputies and journalists, according to an order issued by the parliament's Socialist president, Javier Torres Vela.</p>
